# Room Workspace (Incident Room)

Feature-specific contract for the **in-room** Incident Response workspace only.

Do **not** mix this file with Create Room, Room Settings product pages, or global UX/UI/DS rules.

| Concern | Lives in |
| --- | --- |
| Status = Icon + Color + Label | `01-war-room-ux.mdc` |
| Cards, hierarchy, cyber character (no cyberpunk) | `02-war-room-ui.mdc` |
| Mantine, tokens, no static hex in apps | `03-monosuite-design-system.mdc`, `mantine-direct-usage.mdc` |
| This page layout, regions, room actions, media, mocks | **this file** |

Prototype source of truth for media + room interactions: `.idea/IWR-Design/IWR-Design/index.html` + `app.js`.

---

## 1. Scope

### In scope

- Incident Room page after enter (`apps/monosuite-war-room/src/pages/room/**`)
- Regions listed below
- Pre-Join / Live / Reconnecting / Screen Sharing / No Media / Closed
- Local mock data and local-only interactions (no backend)

### Out of scope

- Create Room flow
- Global nav destinations other than room-active affordances
- Inventing parallel colour systems or hex in the app

---

## 2. Page layout (target)

```
┌─ Global Header (always-dark chrome) ─────────────────────────────┐
├─ Left nav │ MAIN ─────────────────────────────────── │ Tools ────┤
│  (icons)  │ LEFT CONTEXT │ CENTER WORKBENCH          │ RIGHT     │
│           │ Attacker     │ Command + Incident info   │ Partic.   │
│           │ Victim       │ Response Workflow         │ Chat      │
│           │ (+ adapters) │ Investigation & Collab    │ Assets    │
│           │              │ (+ Screen Share / Video)  │ Evidence  │
│           │              │                           │ History   │
├───────────┴──────────────┴───────────────────────────┴───────────┤
└─ Media Control Bar (always-dark chrome, full width) ─────────────┘
```

### Region rules

1. **Global header** — always dark via `--monosuite-color-chrome*`. Does not flip with light/dark scheme.
2. **Media bar** — always dark via the same chrome tokens. Full width under main + tools.
3. **Main workbench + tool panels** — follow light/dark semantic surfaces (`--monosuite-color-background|surface|surface-sunken`, `body`, `default-border`).
4. **Attacker header** — semantic `danger` (never raw hex).
5. **Victim header** — semantic `neutral` / chrome-adjacent dark strip on raised surface; not the same as attacker.
6. Communication must not dominate investigation unless Screen Share or Video is active.

