### 3.15 Floating / docked Media Control Bar

**Implementation reference:** IWR `#media-dock` structure and `renderMediaControls()` behaviour. Use Mantine + chrome tokens — do not paste raw prototype CSS hex.

**Always visible regions**

- Left status: LIVE / LIVE ROOM, participant count, comm note or duration, optional “participants can see your screen”
- Center: Join Live **or** session controls
- Right (when joined): connection mark + label + Retry when lost/reconnecting

**Controls (joined)**

| Control | States |
| --- | --- |
| Microphone | On / Muted |
| Camera | On / Off |
| Speaker | On / Muted |
| Screen Share | Off / Sharing |
| Stop Sharing | Visible only when self-sharing |
| Settings | Opens Media Settings modal |
| More | Test devices, Connection details |

**Media Settings mock devices**

- Mic: Default / Headset USB / Communications Headset
- Speaker: Default / External / Headset Earphone
- Camera: Integrated / Studio / Virtual
- Connection quality select: Good / Fair / Poor (demo)

**Connection cycle (demo):** `connected → poor → reconnecting → lost` (and Retry).

**Initial media state**

```ts
media = {
  joined: false,
  mic: true,
  camera: false,
  speaker: true,
  share: false,
  remoteShareBy: null,
  shareLayout: 'split',
  connection: 'idle',
  speakingId: 'sarah',
}
```

---

### 3.16 Room Actions (summary)

All room-level actions from Command Area + Media More + tool invites funnel to the same mock handlers (toast / local state / history append). Do not invent a second action model.

